<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="it"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="it"/><updated>2026-09-17T17:50:34+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/feed.xml</id><title type="html">CrazyWeb</title><subtitle>CrazyWeb è una Web Agency a Roma dal 2013: comunicazione, web marketing e sviluppo di piattaforme digitali per imprese, start up e Pubblica Amministrazione.</subtitle><entry><title type="html">Servizi CrazyWeb</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/servizi-crazyweb/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Servizi CrazyWeb"/><published>2026-09-17T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-17T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/servizi-crazyweb</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/servizi-crazyweb/"><![CDATA[<p>Elenco dei servizi offerti da CrazyWeb — Web Agency.</p> <h2 id="servizi">Servizi</h2> <ul> <li>Sviluppo siti web</li> <li>Web marketing</li> <li>Comunicazione digitale</li> <li>Sviluppo piattaforme digitali</li> </ul> <p><em>Pagina in aggiornamento: aggiungeremo qui tutti i servizi man mano che li definiamo.</em></p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="generale"/><category term="servizi"/><category term="crazyweb"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Elenco dei servizi offerti da CrazyWeb]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Guida di prova per le categorie</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/guida-di-prova/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Guida di prova per le categorie"/><published>2026-09-14T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-14T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/guida-di-prova</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/guida-di-prova/"><![CDATA[<p>Questo è un articolo di prova per verificare che la categoria assegnata dall’admin compaia correttamente nel breadcrumb sopra il titolo, con link funzionante alla pagina archivio della categoria.</p> <p>Se vedi “Blog / guide / Guida di prova per le categorie” sopra il titolo, tutto funziona come WordPress.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="guide"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Articolo di verifica per il breadcrumb e le categorie stile WordPress]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">nuovo artiolo xy</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/nuovo-artiolo-xy/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="nuovo artiolo xy"/><published>2026-09-14T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-14T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/nuovo-artiolo-xy</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/nuovo-artiolo-xy/"><![CDATA[nuovo artiolo xy test]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="generale"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[nuovo artiolo xy]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">pirmoissimo posto ciao</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/pirmoissimo-posto-ciao/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="pirmoissimo posto ciao"/><published>2026-09-13T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-13T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/pirmoissimo-posto-ciao</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/pirmoissimo-posto-ciao/"><![CDATA[aaa <b>verifica generale</b>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="generale"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[ciao questa è descrizione breve testing grazie love u]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">nuovopostxlm</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/nuovopostxlm/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="nuovopostxlm"/><published>2026-09-12T22:12:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-12T22:12:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/nuovopostxlm</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/nuovopostxlm/"><![CDATA[<p>nuovopostxlm nuovopostxlm</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[nuovopostxlm nuovopostxlm nuovopostxlm]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">nuovopost</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/nuovopost/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="nuovopost"/><published>2026-09-12T22:06:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-12T22:06:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/nuovopost</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/nuovopost/"><![CDATA[<p>nuovopostnuovopostnuovopost nuovopostnuovopostnuovopostnuovopost nuovopost</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="nuovopost"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[nuovopost]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">il post di martino</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/il-post-di-martino/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="il post di martino"/><published>2026-09-12T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-09-12T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/il-post-di-martino</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/il-post-di-martino/"><![CDATA[<p>il post di martino bella<br/></p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="generale"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[il post di martino bella]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">a post with marimo snippets</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/marimo/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="a post with marimo snippets"/><published>2025-04-28T12:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-04-28T12:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/marimo</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/marimo/"><![CDATA[<p><a href="https://marimo.io">marimo</a> notebooks can run Python directly in the reader’s browser. Opt a page in from its front matter:</p> <div class="language-yaml highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="nn">---</span>
<span class="na">layout</span><span class="pi">:</span> <span class="s">post</span>
<span class="na">title</span><span class="pi">:</span> <span class="s">a post with marimo snippets</span>
<span class="na">marimo</span><span class="pi">:</span> <span class="kc">true</span>
<span class="nn">---</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>Nothing is loaded on pages without that flag, so bundling the plugin costs nothing site-wide.</p> <h2 id="runnable-snippets">Runnable snippets</h2> <p>Wrap fenced Python blocks in a container and the runtime turns them into an interactive notebook after the page loads:</p> <div class="al-marimo-inline"> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">marimo</span> <span class="k">as</span> <span class="n">mo</span>

<span class="n">slider</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">mo</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">ui</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">slider</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="mi">20</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">value</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="mi">5</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">label</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">n</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="n">slider</span>
</code></pre></div> </div> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">mo</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">md</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sa">f</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">The first </span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">slider</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">value</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s"> squares: </span><span class="si">{</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">i</span><span class="o">**</span><span class="mi">2</span> <span class="k">for</span> <span class="n">i</span> <span class="ow">in</span> <span class="nf">range</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">slider</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">value</span> <span class="o">+</span> <span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">)]</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div> </div> </div> <p>Until the runtime has moved those blocks into place the container stays hidden, so readers never see the raw source flash before it becomes a notebook.</p> <h2 id="embedding-a-hosted-notebook">Embedding a hosted notebook</h2> <p>If you already publish a notebook — on <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">marimo.app</code> or your own WASM host — embed it instead:</p> <div class="language-liquid highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="cp">{%</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nt">al_marimo_embed</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="na">src</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s2">"https://marimo.app/l/your-notebook"</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="na">height</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s2">"700px"</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="na">caption</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="s2">"Sampling demo"</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="cp">%}</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>The frame is sandboxed <strong>without</strong> <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">allow-same-origin</code>, so the embedded notebook cannot reach this page’s storage or cookies.</p> <h2 id="a-note-on-what-this-loads">A note on what this loads</h2> <p>The <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">marimo-snippets</code> runtime is vendored into the plugin at a pinned version and served from your own site, rather than pulled from a CDN — so no third-party origin executes script in your readers’ pages. Running a notebook does contact marimo’s host, which is worth knowing before you opt a page in.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="sample-posts"/><category term="code"/><category term="formatting"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[running Python in the browser with marimo]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">a post with plotly.js</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/plotly/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="a post with plotly.js"/><published>2025-03-26T14:24:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-03-26T14:24:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/plotly</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/plotly/"><![CDATA[<p>This is an example post with some <a href="https://plotly.com/javascript/">plotly</a> code.</p> <div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="p">```</span><span class="nl">plotly
</span><span class="sb">{
  "data": [
    {
      "x": [1, 2, 3, 4],
      "y": [10, 15, 13, 17],
      "type": "scatter"
    },
    {
      "x": [1, 2, 3, 4],
      "y": [16, 5, 11, 9],
      "type": "scatter"
    }
  ]
}</span>
<span class="p">```</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>Which generates:</p> <pre><code class="language-plotly">{
  "data": [
    {
      "x": [1, 2, 3, 4],
      "y": [10, 15, 13, 17],
      "type": "scatter"
    },
    {
      "x": [1, 2, 3, 4],
      "y": [16, 5, 11, 9],
      "type": "scatter"
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <p>Also another example chart.</p> <div class="language-markdown highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="p">```</span><span class="nl">plotly
</span><span class="sb">{
  "data": [
    {
      "x": [1, 2, 3, 4],
      "y": [10, 15, 13, 17],
      "mode": "markers"
    },
    {
      "x": [2, 3, 4, 5],
      "y": [16, 5, 11, 9],
      "mode": "lines"
    },
    {
      "x": [1, 2, 3, 4],
      "y": [12, 9, 15, 12],
      "mode": "lines+markers"
    }
  ],
  "layout": {
    "title": {
      "text": "Line and Scatter Plot"
    }
  }
}</span>
<span class="p">```</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>This is how it looks like:</p> <pre><code class="language-plotly">{
  "data": [
    {
      "x": [1, 2, 3, 4],
      "y": [10, 15, 13, 17],
      "mode": "markers"
    },
    {
      "x": [2, 3, 4, 5],
      "y": [16, 5, 11, 9],
      "mode": "lines"
    },
    {
      "x": [1, 2, 3, 4],
      "y": [12, 9, 15, 12],
      "mode": "lines+markers"
    }
  ],
  "layout": {
    "title": {
      "text": "Line and Scatter Plot"
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="sample-posts"/><category term="formatting"/><category term="charts"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[this is what included plotly.js code could look like]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">a post with image galleries</title><link href="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/photo-gallery/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="a post with image galleries"/><published>2024-12-04T01:59:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-12-04T01:59:00+00:00</updated><id>https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/photo-gallery</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://cialdecompatibili-netizen.github.io/crazyweb/blog/photo-gallery/"><![CDATA[<p>The images in this post are all zoomable, arranged into different mini-galleries using different libraries.</p> <h2 id="lightbox2">Lightbox2</h2> <p><a href="https://cdn.photoswipe.com/photoswipe-demo-images/photos/1/img-2500.jpg" data-lightbox="roadtrip"><img src="https://cdn.photoswipe.com/photoswipe-demo-images/photos/1/img-200.jpg"/></a> <a href="https://cdn.photoswipe.com/photoswipe-demo-images/photos/2/img-2500.jpg" data-lightbox="roadtrip"><img src="https://cdn.photoswipe.com/photoswipe-demo-images/photos/2/img-200.jpg"/></a> <a href="https://cdn.photoswipe.com/photoswipe-demo-images/photos/3/img-2500.jpg" data-lightbox="roadtrip"><img src="https://cdn.photoswipe.com/photoswipe-demo-images/photos/3/img-200.jpg"/></a></p> <hr/> <h2 id="photoswipe"><a href="https://photoswipe.com/">PhotoSwipe</a></h2> <div class="pswp-gallery pswp-gallery--single-column" id="gallery--getting-started"> <a href="https://cdn.photoswipe.com/photoswipe-demo-images/photos/2/img-2500.jpg" data-pswp-width="1669" data-pswp-height="2500" target="_blank"> <img src="https://cdn.photoswipe.com/photoswipe-demo-images/photos/2/img-200.jpg" alt=""/> </a> <a href="https://cdn.photoswipe.com/photoswipe-demo-images/photos/7/img-2500.jpg" data-pswp-width="1875" 